## potential features

### easy
- install to selected shells, how to detect installed shells?

### medium
- support other shells? (nushell, powershell...)
- markdown rendering (tables at the very least)

### hard
- mermaid graphs render in cli? hardware enabled image?
- smart permissions mode (llm sets it own perms (dangerous.. but less so than full auto?))

- [] non claude backend -> custom agent harness? (stripped down hermes?) 
    - [x] medium qwen3.5-30b-a3b 
    - [] small 7-14b
    - [] tiny 1-3b
    - [] nano 0.5b
    - [] pico 50-300m apple neural engine accel? custom shell agent? (the data transfomration pipeline squeeze out the hardware to the max on m1 chip)
the point is that we are testing this with claude but the real killer is a composable agentic shell program running on something like ANE and trained exactly

we have discovered that the agent harness is just the UNIX environment:
- sh    (1977 - C) shell environment
- perl  (1987 - C) text processing
- curl  (1998 - C) networking
for this environment using RL... (forgot what to say)

global sessions (tailscale) point to one ip where llm is hosted (llama-server mode). It keeps the session data local to itself (how anthropic does resume). But with the same session_id you can have a global session in the sense that you can invoke the same session from multiple PCs. This means multi user sessions and different computer cntexts across one singular session.

